## Summary

**`src/lib.rs`** — added the public function:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact-match on each note's `tags` (via `any`), preserving relative order.

**`src/main.rs`** — wired `--tag <TAG>` into the `list` command. It parses the flag from the remaining args, then routes through `filter_by_tag` when supplied (otherwise lists all). A missing value or unknown flag exits with an error.

**`tests/basic.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag_matches_exact_tag_only` covering order preservation, exact (non-substring) matching, and empty results.

**Verified:** `cargo build` clean, all 3 tests pass, and manual CLI runs confirm the filter behaves as specified. No fixture, benchmark, or sibling checkout was touched.


